abstract: >-
  A prospective, preregistered falsification test of whether an engineered
  experience-dependent state in a frozen simulated reaction-transport droplet
  is a locally owned individual memory. An engineered two-component memory
  field remains decodable and causally active on feeding through deep material
  turnover, yet the target-local representation fails a preregistered ownership
  conjunction (it does not exclude a target-memory-masked environmental summary
  or a body/environment baseline). The frozen decision tree selects Outcome B:
  causal persistence without evidence of local ownership. Within the tested C1c
  architecture, causal persistence is insufficient to establish individual
  memory. No DOI is asserted for this version.
